# S0.2.5 (Article XVII / ARCH-052) — execution evidence manifests.
# The manifest is a GENERATED artifact, not a tracked source file. The
# verifier requires manifest.commit_sha == git rev-parse HEAD; if the
# manifest were committed as a tracked file, the act of committing it
# would advance HEAD and invalidate the manifest (manifest.commit_sha
# would describe the PREVIOUS commit, not the manifest commit).
#
# The directory docs/verification/ is tracked (via README.md files in
# docs/verification/ and docs/verification/history/) so the structure
# exists in the repo. The manifest files themselves are gitignored
# and produced by scripts/generate-execution-evidence.sh (locally) or
# the execution-evidence CI job (in CI, uploaded as an Actions artifact
# with 30-day retention).
/docs/verification/latest-execution.json
/docs/verification/history/*.json
android/.gradle/
android/build/
android/app/build/
android/local.properties
db/custom.db
